            <ArticleTitle>Dipyridamole-induced myocardial ischemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1515-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angina and ischemic electrocardiographic changes occurred after administration of oral dipyridamole in four patients awaiting urgent myocardial revascularization procedures. To our knowledge, this has not previously been reported as a side effect of preoperative dipyridamole therapy, although dipyridamole-induced myocardial ischemia has been demonstrated to occur in animals and humans with coronary artery disease. Epicardial coronary collateral vessels were demonstrated in all four patients; a coronary &quot;steal&quot; phenomenon may be the mechanism of the dipyridamole-induced ischemia observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
